          "ruleId": "CWE-862",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "projects.patch('/:projectId') updates the project's name using only the :projectId URL param, with no check that the project belongs to the caller's ctx.state.orgId. Any authenticated user from any org can rename an arbitrary other org's project just by guessing/enumerating a project id.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): Read the real source and traced the auth middleware myself. packages/backend/src/api/v1/projects/index.ts:91-106 defines `projects.patch(\"/:projectId\", ...)`, which destructures `projectId` only from `ctx.params` (the URL path param) and runs `update project set name = ${name} where id = ${projectId}` with no `org_id`/`ctx.state.orgId` predicate anywhere in the handler. This is an exact mirror of the sibling `projects.delete(\"/:projectId\")` handler's `projectId` source, but unlike `delete` (which at least queries by `org_id` for an unrelated count check) and `projects.post(\"/\")` (which always sets `orgId` on insert via `ctx.state`), the PATCH handler never reads `ctx.state.orgId` at all. I then checked the only org-scoping guard in the request pipeline: `authMiddleware` in packages/backend/src/api/v1/auth/utils.ts (applied globally via `app.use(authMiddleware)` in src/index.ts, before `v1.routes()`). That middleware sets `ctx.state.orgId` from the JWT and only validates org ownership of `ctx.state.projectId`, which it populates solely from `ctx.request.query.projectId` (the query string) or a bearer-token-as-UUID case for public routes (lines 82, 92, 102, 121) \u2014 it never inspects `ctx.params.projectId` (the route param used by the projects router). So for `PATCH /v1/projects/:projectId`, the only org check in the whole stack is skipped entirely: any authenticated user from any org, holding a valid JWT (so not from a public/unauthenticated route \u2014 `/v1/projects/*` is not in `publicRoutes`), can PATCH an arbitrary project id belonging to a different org and rename it. Graph query confirms the static CPG marks this handler (and its get/post/delete siblings in the same file) as `reachable_from_entry=false` uniformly \u2014 consistent with the documented limitation that koa-router `.verb()` arrow-function callbacks are under-linked by the static graph, not with the route actually being dead code (it is wired up live via `v1.use(projects.routes())` \u2192 `app.use(v1.routes())`)."
